## Why This Is Asked

This question tests real-world log ingestion across mixed formats, including gzipped archives and unreadable files. It assesses the ability to perform per-hour bucketing and cross-format parsing without external dependencies, while handling missing or malformed fields gracefully.

## Key Concepts

- POSIX shell pipelines
- Transparent gzip handling with zcat
- Format-agnostic parsing (regex for plain text + JSON field extraction)
- Per-hour bucketing and aggregation using awk associative arrays

## Code Example

```bash
find /logs -type f \( -name '*.log' -o -name '*.log.gz' \) 2>/dev/null |
  while read -r f; do
    [ -r "$f" ] || continue
    case "$f" in
      *.gz) zcat "$f" 2>/dev/null ;;
      *) cat "$f" 2>/dev/null ;;
    esac
  done |
  awk '
    /^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}/ {
      hour = substr($1,1,13)
      match($0, / (INFO|WARN|ERROR):/, m)
      if (m[1]) counts[hour,m[1]]++
    }
    /^\{/ {
      if (match($0, /"ts":"([^"]+)"/, t) && match($0, /"lvl":"([^"]+)"/, l)) {
        hour = substr(t[1],1,13)
        counts[hour,l[1]]++
      }
    }
    END {
      for (i=0;i<24;i++) {
        h = strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H", systime() - i*3600)
        printf "%s: INFO=%d WARN=%d ERROR=%d\n", h, counts[h,"INFO"]+0, counts[h,"WARN"]+0, counts[h,"ERROR"]+0
      }
    }
  '
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical log parsing under rotation, mixed formats, gz archives, and multi-line blocks. It also checks ability to design robust pipelines with standard UNIX tools.

## Key Concepts
- POSIX text processing (awk, sed)
- gzipped logs via zcat
- JSON vs text parsing
- multi-line block handling
- time bucketing by hour

## Code Example
```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
cutoff=$(date -d '6 hours ago' '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')
zcat /logs/app/**/*.log.gz /logs/app/**/*.log 2>/dev/null | awk -v c="$cutoff" '
  function hour(ts){ return substr(ts,1,13) }
  {
    if($0 ~ /"ts":/) { match($0, /"ts":"([^\"]+)"/, m); ts=m[1]; match($0, /"src":"([^\"]+)"/, s); ip=s[1] }
    else if($0 ~ /^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}/) { ts=$1" "$2 }
    if(ts && ip && /FAILED/){ h=hour(ts); buckets[h][ip]=1 }
  }
  END{ for (h in buckets) print h, length(buckets[h]) }
'
```

